103:Column 0 of the explorer tree takes `datatable.IndicatorColumn`; the spinner in `iconCell` goes. Decisions: (Q0-A) *registry only, no `WantsBlink`*: a group loading its children keeps the footer line, since `TreeNode.Loading` is never drawn on a visible row. (Q1-C) *a failed create is an event only*: the placeholder is dropped, the cause is the footer error and the failed run in `:jobs`; a create failure is read on placeholder rows only, so a healthy row is never marked `⊗`. A failed delete keeps its row with `⊗` until the next attempt. (Q2-A) *`jobs.NewImmediateRun`* admits a run already running (a create or delete has nothing in front of it), so `:jobs` shows `●` and greys `K`; `ws` delete and `:files` delete keep `NewRun` and the defect, tracked in DEVDESK-227. Hypotheses: kinds per row are `delete` everywhere and `create` on placeholders; in selection mode a failed row shows its checkbox; guards (`busy`, `actionable`) unchanged; events use `components.FailureEvent`; no per-frame rebuild. The clone list stays on `jobFrame` until A-10b.
